// TARGET rules for the CASHBOOK app (project recat-auth-test).
// DO NOT APPLY YET - see the blocker below.
//
// Comments are // lines, not "//" keys. Firebase accepts exactly one
// top-level property, "rules", and reads every key inside it as a child
// node, so a "//" entry is rejected outright ("Expected '{'"). The earlier
// draft of this file used five of them and could never have been applied.
//
// BLOCKER, measured rather than assumed
// scripts/audit-membership.mjs against the live database (2026-11-12):
//
//     11 shops | READY 1 | MAPPABLE 1 | NO-UID 9
//
// Only ONE shop has a members map. Nine have no Firebase Auth identity at
// all: they were created by cashbook/auth/index.html, which writes the
// password into the database (:125) and compares it in the browser (:141).
// There is no uid for a members map to be keyed by, so no amount of logging
// in will self-claim them. Applying these rules now locks out 10 of 11 shops
// permanently, which is the precise failure the audit warns about.
//
// Order of work, therefore:
//   1. Move the nine password-in-database shops onto Firebase Auth. Until
//      that happens these rules cannot be applied at all.
//   2. Backfill members for them and for "mobi fixer" (MAPPABLE).
//   3. Re-run the audit. Only when it reports READY for every shop, set
//      ENFORCE_MEMBERSHIP = true in cashbook/main.js and apply this file.
//
// Separately and more urgently: while /users is world-readable, those nine
// passwords are readable by anyone on the internet. No database rule fixes
// that - the field has to stop being stored.
//
// UNRESOLVED in the rules below
//   - loginUser reads /users/$shop BEFORE signing in, which these rules deny.
//   - /feedback and /auditLogs are not covered, so the root deny applies and
//     the app's writes to them would start failing.
//   - The $shop wildcard at the root also matches authAudit, feedback,
//     auditLogs and clicks; for those root.child('users').child($shop) does
//     not exist, so they are denied by accident rather than by design.
// None of these are safe to leave as they are; they are listed so the next
// pass over this file starts from the real list.
{
  "rules": {
    ".read": false,
    ".write": false,

    "users": {
      "$shop": {
        ".read": "auth != null && data.child('members').child(auth.uid).exists()",
        ".write": "auth != null && (data.child('members').child(auth.uid).exists() || !data.exists())",

        // Public lookup so a member can find the shop before signing in.
        "signupInfo": {
          "email": { ".read": true }
        }
      }
    },

    // The ledger itself: {username}/{YYYY-MM-DD}/{in|out|liquid}, plus
    // goals/reminders/recycleBin/counters.
    "$shop": {
      ".read": "auth != null && root.child('users').child($shop).child('members').child(auth.uid).exists()",
      ".write": "auth != null && root.child('users').child($shop).child('members').child(auth.uid).exists()"
    }
  }
}
